Let $x,$ $y,$ $z$ be nonnegative real numbers satisfying $x \leq 1$, $y \leq 2$, and $z \leq 3$. Define
\begin{align*}
C &= \sqrt{x + 3} + \sqrt{y + 6} + \sqrt{z + 12}, \\
D &= \sqrt{x + 1} + \sqrt{y + 2} + \sqrt{z + 3}.
\end{align*}
Find the minimum value of $C^2 - D^2.$
